    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nConverting a FormData with a normal nested field named `length` throws `RangeError: Invalid array length`. This affects `axios.formToJSON()` and posting FormData with `Content-Type: application/json`.\n\n### To reproduce\n\n```js\nimport axios from 'axios';\n\nconst form = new FormData();\nform.append('metadata[length]', 'long');\nconsole.log(axios.formToJSON(form));\n```\n\nActual: `RangeError: Invalid array length`.\n\nExpected: `{ metadata: { length: 'long' } }`.\n\nThe dot form `metadata.length`, repeated `metadata[length]` values and `metadata[length][unit]` also fail. These names can come directly from ordinary HTML form inputs.\n\n### Environment\n\nAxios `v1.x` at `6576f5753e26444d8d04b0a7c0b4d9d0a83bdaa0`, Node 22.22.1 and Linux. The issue is in the shared FormData-to-JSON parser: an intermediate array receives the named `length` key before it can be converted to an object. A focused fix can convert that intermediate array before descending into `length` while preserving any numeric siblings.\n\nAI assistance was used to investigate this report.\n",
